#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:42
#: 
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:5
#: f7de526aac8b4725a9325c236a6f2ec5
msgid "Firmware Limitations on AutoPilot Hardware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:7
#: f2df851b981542ceb4275db09c46e144
msgid "The ArduPilot firmware in some configurations exceeds 1 MB in size. Some autopilots may not have enough flash memory to store the full firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:9
#: 5014a0bf657d46efac8218a971e7eddb
msgid "For the affected autopilots, a reduced firmware is generated. This firmware omits less-commonly used features in order to reduce the firmware size to less than 1 MB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:11
#: b6fd5ba774b24f23bd44cbe8f24db2c0
msgid "|ss| :ref:`The missing features are listed on this page<binary-features>` for each board type for the current \"latest\" firmware. If you require any of these features, you can try to create a build with them in it (at the expense of other non-needed features) using the `Custom Firmware Build Server <https://custom.ardupilot.org>`__. The missing features list for a board are listed in the same groups and labels as those shown on the Custom Firmware Build Server. |se|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:13
#: 97f381f3f79f461e8b5c4c955d8040b2
msgid "Currently the above page of missing features is auto-generated and has a bug, While this is being investigated and corrected, the definitive list for a given board and firmware version can be found in its firmware folder on `the firmware server <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/>`__ in its \"features.txt' file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:15
#: 3803e59f3b0948598066875092634f1e
msgid "Using the server does require you to know which features you DO want to have and check them, as well as the ones desired that are currently missing. A table of all current build options that can be selected are shown :ref:`here<all-features>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:21
#: 2e325353a09745f782eac5c891bbd969
msgid "RAM Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:23
#: 62f147db47f344d6a439da6c8049997a
msgid "There may be insufficient RAM available in some autopilots to support all enabled firmware features. Some possible symptoms are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:25
#: 08ebeaaab9064a9382e8cec0c3215166
msgid "MAVFTP does not work. Parameter downloads to GCS are delayed starting while the GCS tries to establish a MAVFTP link which cannot be setup, and then proceed slowly to download parameters using the normal download method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:26
#: 84f6192d42844a58951dc71a88dce910
msgid "Compass Calibration will not start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:27
#: fd39d17b07f94c2b80bc5d6704d0b3ae
msgid "Logging will not start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:28
#: 17d067761f6e48c4ac0177f74c9ad9f4
msgid "Terrain downloading from GCS will not start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:29
#: 85249ffd45bd42938d173d1023ade51d
msgid "Interfaces will not initialize, such as CAN: \"Failed to initialise CAN Interface xx\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:31
#: b78098de2b74432a96824b7582cc4612
msgid "If this occurs, several possible options are available to allow temporary use of MAVFTP, download terrain tiles, allow a driver to be loaded, and/or Compass Calibration. All require a reboot to take effect:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:33
#: fe6230594556449898ab899493e3e9bf
msgid "Make sure IMU Batch Sampling (used for FFT analysis) is not running by setting :ref:`INS_LOG_BAT_MASK<INS_LOG_BAT_MASK>` = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:34
#: d457bdc7c921452ba250f6ebd2b9bdb9
msgid "Try temporarily disabling logging by setting :ref:`LOG_BACKEND_TYPE<LOG_BACKEND_TYPE>` to 0, then returning to 1 (default) after calibrating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:35
#: 044e4340170c4feba218c8c7f372936b
msgid "Reduce the size of :ref:`LOG_FILE_BUFSIZE<LOG_FILE_BUFSIZE>`. However, lowering below 16KB can introduce small gaps in the log. This may be used temporarily to download terrain or calibrate compass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:36
#: 852f65e75f4847e2a819c575d5d52aa1
msgid "Disable Terrain Following temporarily by setting :ref:`TERRAIN_ENABLE<TERRAIN_ENABLE>` to 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:37
#: 4f3bef56203f49d6a0af5cd9d62d3b1f
msgid "Disable SmartRTL on Copter by setting :ref:`SRTL_POINTS<SRTL_POINTS>` = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:38
#: 6967cb3aa7f3445ea926a72bd0847bde
msgid "If using DroneCAN, try reducing the memory allocation from the default of 16KB (for two nodes) using the ``CAN_Dx_UC_POOL`` parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-limited-firmware.rst:40
#: 48e829ae98cb47f2921748a73930c67d
msgid "in Mission Planner's STATUS tab, you can monitor the \"freemem\" status for current free RAM. Be aware, that it's a total of unallocated memory and that everything that requires a memory allocation needs it to be one, contiguous block. But the status will give an indication of what is available. For example, MAVftp needs ~ 12K contiguous block to start."
msgstr ""
